{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in specifications. The policy keeps clear-space behavior biased to forward progress, inserts only brief random-walk variation, uses directed one-shot turns for side obstacles, uses a rare one-shot backward escape only for front blockage, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort stuck state after repeated blocked outcomes.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion so specifications can bind sensor outcomes to exactly one safe action per decision state",
    "Use one-shot commit/recovery states with obstacle events able to preempt only when safety-critical, and return to forward exploration immediately on path_clear"
  ],
